<figure class="card-diagram">
  <div class="card-diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      class="topology"
      viewBox="0 0 820 400"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="ai-workflow-title ai-workflow-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
    >
      <title id="ai-workflow-title">What happens before a coding agent writes a line</title>
      <desc id="ai-workflow-desc">
        Five steps and a sub-step, then a hand-off. One: initial prompting —
        research, breaking an oversized task into phases, and discussing
        guardrails and security, usually with a free-tier sub-agent rather
        than the coding agent. Two: prompt refining — the draft is cut down
        to only the words, phrases, constraints and context the task needs,
        which costs fewer tokens and produces fewer clarifying questions
        later. Three: the orchestrator matches the task to a model and an
        effort level — low for a small task, high for a hard or
        high-consequence one, on purpose. Four: for medium or large work, a
        planning phase runs on a higher model at high to ultra effort; the
        refined prompt and the retrieved context docs are fed to the coding
        agent, which can ask the orchestrator for clarification. Step four
        point one, simplified RAG, sits inside planning: an indexed router
        retrieves only the documents the task needs and loads any AI skill
        the task calls for on demand. Five: the orchestrator reviews the
        plan as the specification, refines or approves it, and stays aware
        of context window, hallucination risk and token usage while doing
        it. From there the flow hands off to the QA card's loop —
        implementation, testing and fixes.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="ai-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="arrow-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" stroke="none" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="research" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 1, initial prompting — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="64">1 · Initial prompting</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="82">research, scope into phases</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="98">guardrails &amp; security first</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M261,82 L287,82" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="refine" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 2, prompt refining — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="64">2 · Prompt refining</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="82">cut to only what's needed</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="98">fewer tokens, fewer questions</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M533,82 L559,82" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="route" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 3, model and effort matched to the task — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="64">3 · Model and effort</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="82">match model tier to task</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="98">complexity, not habit</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M682,124 L682,230" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="plan" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 4, planning phase — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="254">4 · Planning phase</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="272">medium/large tasks only</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="288">high effort when it counts</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M559,272 L533,272" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="rag" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 4 point 1, simplified RAG — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="254">4.1 · Simplified RAG</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="272">router retrieves the docs</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="288">skills load on demand</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M287,272 L261,272" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="review" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 5, orchestrator review and approval — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="254">5 · Review and approve</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="272">plan becomes the spec</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="288">orchestrator signs off</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M138,314 L138,338" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />
      <text class="wire accent" x="150" y="332">hands off to</text>
      <text class="wire accent" x="150" y="346">the QA cycle from here</text>

      <text class="wire accent" x="15" y="368">1.6k lines across 13 documents</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="384">a common task loads the entry doc plus 1–2 more — zero repo-wide search.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="card-diagram-caption">
